# Weatherglass Shoal - an island of the library's plan The Gravity Sea (a side island at sea level, km 5, ahead)
# A low sandy shoal with the Institute's weather station: a boardwalk on posts from the beach, the Stevenson screen (a
# slatted box on four legs), the great glass barometer (a glass-tinted ice pillar) and the station's chest. Quest "The
# Weatherglass" (5 steps): the station, the weather log, the barometer's reading, the station chest and the twin note -
# which tells of the station's drowned twin, just north (Weatherglass Deep, near:shoal:600:north).
#
# Built by the recipe player (CIRecipe weatherglass_shoal) through the editor's own operations. Points (metres over the
# water line): the station's flat at 2.5 m (r 7 round 0 2); the boardwalk x -12..-3, z -12..-10.5, deck 1.2 m over the
# beach shelf at 0.3 m; the screen at 3 4, the barometer at -3 4.
include lib_sea
include lib_features
include lib_huts
include lib_gravity
new
gen Trees=0.05 Bushes=0.25 Rocks=0.2 Harvest=0.3 BeachThings=0.4
gen Seed=9721 Radius=24 Height=4 Roughness=0.25 Peaks=1 Shape=0 Style=0 PeakShape=0.3 Cliffs=0.2 BeachWidth=0.8
gen Water=0.5 SeaRocks=0.3 SeaFinds=0.3 Sunken=0.2 Hostiles=0 Friendly=0.2 SeaLife=0.3
generate

# --- Terrain: the station's flat, the beach shelf under the boardwalk -----------------------------------------------
brush flatten at 0 2 r=7 s=20 frames=200 h=2.5
brush flatten from -13 -11 to -3 -11 r=2.5 s=20 frames=120 h=0.3
origin
clear at 0 2 r=6
clear at -8 -11 r=4

# --- The boardwalk from the beach towards the station ----------------------------------------------------------------
push at -12 -12 h=0.3
call boardwalk n=6 wide=1 y=1.2
pop

# --- The weather station: the Stevenson screen, the barometer, the log, the chest ----------------------------------
place RT_Pillar screenlegs at 2.8 3.8 ground sy=0.4
place RT_Pillar screenlegs at 3.2 3.8 ground sy=0.4
place RT_Pillar screenlegs at 2.8 4.2 ground sy=0.4
place RT_Pillar screenlegs at 3.2 4.2 ground sy=0.4
place "Box Small" screen at 3 4 ground y=0.95 sit
prop screen tint.color=#e8e4d8
prop screen tint.amount=0.6
place TP_IcePillar01 barometer at -3 4 ground sit scale=0.35
prop barometer tint.color=#bfe4ee
prop barometer tint.amount=0.6
place Note_Sign weatherlog at 0 -2 ground sit yaw=180
place Loot_Chest stationchest at 1 6.5 ground sit yaw=180
place "Box Small" - at -1.2 6.6 ground sit
place Note_Paper twinnote at -1.2 6.6 ground y=0.7 drop yaw=20
place Zone_Trigger stationzone at 0 0 ground y=1

# --- Things to gather ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
call shallows x=0 z=0 r=36 deep=5 n=1 seed=9731
call dirt x=8 z=-4 r=5 n=2 seed=9732

# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ----------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Weatherglass Shoal
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A low shoal with the Halvard Institute's weather station: a boardwalk, a Stevenson screen and a great glass barometer. A side island of The Gravity Sea - its twin lies drowned just north.
island on.arrive=message||A sandbank with a boardwalk, a white box on legs - and a glass column taller than a man, shining.

story reading|Barometer reading|Note_Paper|The great barometer's reading: "FIELD 1.8 - FALLING NORTH".

note weatherlog Weather log | WEATHERGLASS STATION - LOG\n\nWind W 3. Sea slight. Field 1.8, steady.\nSince Lift Day the barometer reads the field, not the weather - Halvard's men rebuilt it.\nTap the glass for a reading.
note stationchest Station chest | The station's chest: the keeper's rations and a spare battery for the barometer.
note twinnote Twin note | TO THE TWIN STATION\n\nThere were two stations, one on each sandbank. On Lift Day the north bank went down, station and all - 20 m under, just north of here.\nIf the field ever falls, someone should dive and read the twin's last log.
loot stationchest Cooked_Mackerel*2;Cooked_Potato*2;Battery*1
prop stationchest loot.refill=0

prop barometer obj.name=barometer
prop barometer beh.use=Tap the barometer's glass
prop barometer if.use=!signal|reading
prop barometer on.use=signal||reading\ngive||story:reading*1\nmessage||The column shivers and settles: FIELD 1.8 - FALLING NORTH.
prop barometer else.use=message||The glass reads the same: FIELD 1.8 - FALLING NORTH.
prop stationzone zone.id=station
prop stationzone zone.radius=4
prop stationzone zone.message=The weather station. The glass column hums faintly.

quest title=The Weatherglass
quest intro=A weather station on a shoal. Walk the boardwalk to it.
step reach|station|1|Walk to the weather station
step read|Weather log|1|Read the station's weather log
step collect|story:reading|1|Take a reading from the great barometer
step open|Station chest|1|Open the station chest
step read|Twin note|1|Read the note to the twin station
quest done=The twin station lies drowned just north of the shoal, 20 m down.
quest reward=Cooked_Mackerel*2;Battery*1

# Buried treasure (reach audit 10-24: a late island of its story line needs one): the metal detector finds it, the shovel digs it
call treasure x=0 z=0 r=18 n=1 seed=8863
prop treasure8863 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*2
# Animals (reach audit 10-24: a late island of its story line had none)
place Creature_Turtle turtles at -21 12 h=-1
prop turtles creature.count=2

save Weatherglass Shoal
